1
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:03,968
[Apocalypse Log 3]

2
00:01:58,917 --> 00:02:00,626
Thank you, bro.

3
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:12,665
What are you doing?

4
00:02:15,456 --> 00:02:17,166
Lin Zai.

5
00:02:17,166 --> 00:02:19,500
Why didn't you say you were hurt?

6
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:21,129
It's just a minor injury.

7
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:33,923
Thank you for your help.

8
00:02:33,923 --> 00:02:36,248
We need to get back to camp quickly.

9
00:02:36,248 --> 00:02:39,706
This bag of supplies will be your reward.

10
00:02:39,706 --> 00:02:41,540
I don't need your supplies.

11
00:02:46,623 --> 00:02:49,206
Lin Zai's foot is injured,
so he definitely can't walk.

12
00:02:49,206 --> 00:02:50,292
And you're seriously injured.

13
00:02:50,292 --> 00:02:52,542
I can't carry the supplies and Lin Zai.

14
00:02:52,542 --> 00:02:54,748
If we encounter danger on the way back,

15
00:02:54,748 --> 00:02:57,028
I'm afraid we won't be able to handle it.

16
00:03:07,706 --> 00:03:09,232
Lead the way.

17
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:21,748
We owe our lives to him today.

18
00:03:21,748 --> 00:03:23,498
If you're sure he's not a threat,

19
00:03:23,498 --> 00:03:25,415
ask him if he'd like to join our camp.

20
00:03:25,415 --> 00:03:27,030
I agree.

21
00:03:32,715 --> 00:03:34,840
Thank you for saving us today.

22
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,257
You saved me last time.

23
00:03:36,257 --> 00:03:37,423
I'm returning the favor.

24
00:03:37,423 --> 00:03:39,132
Now, we're even.

25
00:03:39,132 --> 00:03:40,798
See? I told you.

26
00:03:40,798 --> 00:03:42,560
Good deeds are rewarded.

27
00:03:45,340 --> 00:03:48,048
I almost thought I'd die today.

28
00:03:48,048 --> 00:03:49,298
No.

29
00:03:49,298 --> 00:03:51,174
It might have been worse than death.

30
00:03:52,715 --> 00:03:54,423
What's your name?

31
00:03:54,423 --> 00:03:57,917
I'm Lin Zai. "Lin" for forest,
"Zai" for the present.

32
00:03:57,917 --> 00:03:59,965
"Lie," as in fire.

33
00:03:59,965 --> 00:04:01,257
Lie.

34
00:04:01,257 --> 00:04:03,048
That's cool.

35
00:04:03,048 --> 00:04:04,840
Do you usually work alone?

36
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:06,423
How did you find us?

37
00:04:06,423 --> 00:04:08,048
You're very noisy.

38
00:04:08,048 --> 00:04:09,757
I'm talking to distract myself.

39
00:04:09,757 --> 00:04:11,583
Otherwise, the pain will kill me.

40
00:04:13,048 --> 00:04:15,034
Hey, watch the road.

41
00:04:51,423 --> 00:04:52,956
Slow down.

42
00:04:53,673 --> 00:04:55,282
Be gentle.

43
00:05:02,340 --> 00:05:04,014
Don't move.

44
00:05:08,507 --> 00:05:10,423
How did this happen?

45
00:05:10,423 --> 00:05:13,264
You were fine when you left.

46
00:05:15,257 --> 00:05:16,257
Grandma.

47
00:05:16,257 --> 00:05:17,299
It's okay.

48
00:05:17,299 --> 00:05:19,923
Look, we're all back in one piece.

49
00:05:19,923 --> 00:05:22,340
Yes, thanks to this bro here.

50
00:05:22,340 --> 00:05:24,632
Hey, bro. Need a hand?

51
00:05:24,632 --> 00:05:27,507
Li, can you knock me out?

52
00:05:27,507 --> 00:05:29,132
Even if I knock you out now,

53
00:05:29,132 --> 00:05:30,340
when I clean your wound later,

54
00:05:30,340 --> 00:05:32,506
you'll still wake up from the pain.

55
00:05:34,590 --> 00:05:36,048
Wait.

56
00:05:38,631 --> 00:05:39,674
Wait, hang on.

57
00:05:39,674 --> 00:05:41,631
Let me get ready first.

58
00:05:53,465 --> 00:05:54,628
You...

59
00:05:55,548 --> 00:05:58,298
I said, let me get ready first.

60
00:05:58,298 --> 00:06:00,422
You didn't give me any warnings!

61
00:06:16,090 --> 00:06:19,617
Hey, your technique is very professional.

62
00:06:21,250 --> 00:06:22,875
I'm used to it.

63
00:06:30,465 --> 00:06:31,882
You've all worked hard.

64
00:06:31,882 --> 00:06:34,423
I'll go make something nice for you.

65
00:06:34,423 --> 00:06:35,923
I'll go.

66
00:06:35,923 --> 00:06:37,423
You stay and take care of them.

67
00:07:36,465 --> 00:07:38,590
This guy is really an all-rounder.

68
00:07:38,590 --> 00:07:41,007
He's truly a god in my eyes.

69
00:07:41,923 --> 00:07:42,925
You're not bad either.

70
00:07:42,925 --> 00:07:46,596
You're getting more skilled
with dressing wounds.

71
00:07:46,596 --> 00:07:47,917
Of course.

72
00:07:47,917 --> 00:07:50,257
Am I a god too?

73
00:07:50,257 --> 00:07:51,757
You're crazy.

74
00:08:05,715 --> 00:08:06,757
Hey, buddy.

75
00:08:06,757 --> 00:08:09,005
Your skills are truly amazing.

76
00:08:14,340 --> 00:08:17,208
Thanks again for your help today.

77
00:08:17,208 --> 00:08:19,437
I apologize for what happened before.

78
00:08:20,257 --> 00:08:21,882
We both got what we needed.

79
00:08:21,882 --> 00:08:23,617
We're even.

80
00:08:35,548 --> 00:08:37,173
The generator's acting up again. I'll check it.

81
00:08:37,173 --> 00:08:39,007
Okay.

82
00:08:39,007 --> 00:08:40,548
Sit still.

83
00:08:40,548 --> 00:08:42,231
Do you want to lose your foot?

84
00:08:44,215 --> 00:08:45,757
I'm the only one who can fix it.

85
00:08:45,757 --> 00:08:47,721
It's an old problem, no trouble at all.

86
00:08:49,298 --> 00:08:50,500
I'll fix it.

87
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:52,507
Where is it?

88
00:08:52,507 --> 00:08:54,048
You? Fix it?

89
00:08:54,048 --> 00:08:56,340
Hey, why don't you two go together?

90
00:08:56,340 --> 00:08:58,222
Stop dawdling. Here.

91
00:09:00,340 --> 00:09:02,590
It's just over there.
I don't want to trouble you.

92
00:09:33,257 --> 00:09:38,257
Aside from being a bit quiet
and looking a bit aloof,

93
00:09:38,257 --> 00:09:41,016
he's perfect in every way.

94
00:09:41,667 --> 00:09:43,840
If he's willing to join our camp,

95
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:46,048
that would be great news.

96
00:09:46,048 --> 00:09:49,465
Lin Zai has really found a treasure.

97
00:09:50,257 --> 00:09:54,340
Maybe we can have Lin Zai
find a chance to ask him again.

98
00:09:54,340 --> 00:09:56,298
If he doesn't want to stay,

99
00:09:56,298 --> 00:10:00,093
we'll give him some supplies
and send him on his way.

100
00:10:00,715 --> 00:10:02,007
Good idea.

101
00:11:25,423 --> 00:11:27,215
Done! All fixed!

102
00:11:27,215 --> 00:11:29,298
Come eat!

103
00:13:17,635 --> 00:13:20,113
It'll be miserable if you catch a cold.

104
00:13:24,048 --> 00:13:25,535
Why are you...

105
00:13:26,257 --> 00:13:29,423
Did you think you were being quiet all night?

106
00:13:32,507 --> 00:13:34,173
I'm sorry.

107
00:13:37,090 --> 00:13:39,048
Does your foot still hurt?

108
00:13:39,798 --> 00:13:41,632
It's much better now.

109
00:13:42,250 --> 00:13:44,798
Why don't you go and rest?

110
00:13:44,798 --> 00:13:47,080
I'll go back and catch up on sleep
when it's light out.

111
00:13:48,298 --> 00:13:49,583
It's fine.

112
00:13:49,583 --> 00:13:51,465
Your camp is very safe.

113
00:13:51,465 --> 00:13:54,173
Just being here is a form of rest.

114
00:13:56,007 --> 00:14:00,022
It seems you haven't had a very easy life...

115
00:14:00,798 --> 00:14:02,625
if this is enough to satisfy you.

116
00:14:12,048 --> 00:14:13,792
My home...

117
00:14:13,792 --> 00:14:16,572
It used to be right along this coastline.

118
00:14:19,132 --> 00:14:21,427
About five or six kilometers to the east.

119
00:14:22,757 --> 00:14:24,445
The house was small.

120
00:14:25,548 --> 00:14:30,481
My parents, me, and my brother.

121
00:14:31,809 --> 00:14:34,038
The four of us lived in that small space.

122
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:38,590
Life was tough,

123
00:14:39,798 --> 00:14:42,090
but we had many beautiful memories.

124
00:14:45,007 --> 00:14:46,681
You haven't gone back to see it?

125
00:14:49,298 --> 00:14:51,472
I'm the only one left alive.

126
00:14:53,298 --> 00:14:55,079
When the apocalypse hit,

127
00:14:56,882 --> 00:14:58,955
my parents didn't make it.

128
00:15:02,590 --> 00:15:06,656
Later, I watched my brother
die right in front of me.

129
00:15:09,298 --> 00:15:11,117
Even if I go back to that house,

130
00:15:12,632 --> 00:15:14,507
I can't go back to the old days.

131
00:15:23,215 --> 00:15:25,477
Life still has to go on.

132
00:15:29,333 --> 00:15:30,763
I know.

133
00:15:32,128 --> 00:15:34,381
I just miss them so much.

134
00:15:36,423 --> 00:15:39,251
They used to put me first in everything.

135
00:15:40,923 --> 00:15:42,715
Especially my brother.

136
00:15:43,923 --> 00:15:45,554
He protected me the most.

137
00:15:49,965 --> 00:15:52,257
If only I had your skills...

138
00:15:54,465 --> 00:15:56,341
Then I could have protected him.

139
00:16:02,048 --> 00:16:04,019
His death...

140
00:16:04,019 --> 00:16:05,501
It wasn't your fault.

141
00:16:11,423 --> 00:16:13,380
In the face of disaster,

142
00:16:14,706 --> 00:16:16,555
we all did our best.

143
00:17:00,423 --> 00:17:01,548
Look.

144
00:17:02,215 --> 00:17:03,882
The sun is rising.

145
00:17:14,923 --> 00:17:16,465
Lie.

146
00:17:16,465 --> 00:17:18,232
Do you want to stay with us?

147
00:17:30,298 --> 00:17:33,083
I still have important things to do.

148
00:17:39,048 --> 00:17:41,086
I was just asking.

149
00:17:48,125 --> 00:17:50,715
Anyway, it's dawn now.

150
00:17:51,507 --> 00:17:53,419
I'm going back to catch up on some sleep.

151
00:17:54,215 --> 00:17:55,984
Make yourself at home.

